# Mollusk / SBF integration tests

Aggregator program tests are **Mollusk SBF tests**. They load compiled BPF **`.so`** binaries from `target/deploy/`. They do **not** run from `cargo check`, `cargo test` without `test-sbf`, or plain `cargo build`.

## What agents get wrong

| Mistake | Reality |
|--------|---------|
| `cargo test -p spamm_aggregator` | Test crate is `#![cfg(feature = "test-sbf")]` — **no tests run** without `--features test-sbf`. |
| `cargo check` then assume tests pass | Check only validates Rust; Mollusk needs **`.so`** files on disk. |
| Expect one `cargo build` to produce everything | **Two** separate `cargo build-sbf` builds (aggregator, MM). |
| Edit MM program, only rebuild aggregator | Stale MM: harness copies from `market_maker/program/target/deploy/spamm_market_maker.so`. |
| Parallel tests on Windows | File-lock errors copying `.so` — use `--test-threads=1`. |
| `cargo build-sbf` aggregator for mainnet without disabling defaults | Default features include `devnet`; mainnet deploy needs `--no-default-features --features bpf-entrypoint,mainnet`. |

## Prerequisites

Solana/Agave toolchain with **`cargo build-sbf`** on PATH (same as `solana --version` install). `target/` is gitignored; `.so` files are **local build artifacts**, never committed.

## Two artifacts (all required)

| Program | Build manifest | Output `.so` |
|---------|----------------|--------------|
| Aggregator | `aggregator/program/Cargo.toml` | `aggregator/program/target/deploy/spamm_aggregator.so` |
| Example MM | `market_maker/program/Cargo.toml` | `market_maker/program/target/deploy/spamm_market_maker.so` |

## How the harness loads them

`tests/spamm_mollusk/common/env.rs` → `Env::new()`:

1. Sets `SBF_OUT_DIR` to `aggregator/program/target/deploy`.
2. **Copies** the newest aggregator `.so` from `target/deploy` or `target/sbpfv3-solana-solana/release` into deploy.
3. **Copies** the newest MM `.so` among `market_maker/program/target/deploy`, `market_maker/.../sbpfv3-solana-solana/release`, and aggregator `target/deploy` / `sbpfv3` release into `aggregator/program/target/deploy/spamm_market_maker.so`.
4. Requires both `.so` files in deploy (after sync).
5. Panics with the exact `cargo build-sbf` commands if any file is missing.

Mollusk registers programs by **filename stem** (`spamm_aggregator`, `spamm_market_maker`), not by path.

## Build (from repo root)

Run both after changing **any** on-chain program code under test:

```powershell
cargo build-sbf --arch v3 --manifest-path aggregator/program/Cargo.toml --features devnet
cargo build-sbf --arch v3 --manifest-path market_maker/program/Cargo.toml
```

For mainnet deploys: `--no-default-features --features bpf-entrypoint,mainnet`. Devnet is the default (`devnet` is in `[features] default`).

Rebuild **only** the crate you changed if you know the other is fresh:

- Aggregator ix/helpers/state → first command only (plus re-run tests).
- `market_maker/program` → second command (harness syncs MM into aggregator deploy dir at test start).

## Run tests

From `aggregator/program`:

```powershell
cargo test -p spamm_aggregator --features test-sbf --test spamm_mollusk -- --test-threads=1
```

- **`--features test-sbf`** — required; enables the test crate, program `log`, and `devnet` cluster constants.
- **`--test-threads=1`** — recommended on Windows (deploy-dir copy mutex; parallel runs can hit “file in use”).
- Filter one module: append `ix_settle_freebet` (or any `mod` name from `tests/spamm_mollusk/main.rs`).

`cargo check -p spamm_aggregator` is fine for fast compile-only validation; it does **not** substitute for the flow above.

## CU ledger

`tests/spamm_mollusk/cu_ledger.md` is regenerated when tests run. Optional full regen uses `--test-threads=4` on Unix; prefer `--test-threads=1` on Windows.

## Agent workflow after program edits

1. `cargo check -p spamm_aggregator --features devnet` (and `-p spamm_market_maker` if MM touched).
2. `cargo build-sbf --arch v3` for each changed program (see table; aggregator needs `--features devnet` or `mainnet`).
3. `cargo test -p spamm_aggregator --features test-sbf --test spamm_mollusk -- --test-threads=1` with a focused filter when possible.
4. If panic says **Missing SBF artifacts**, run the two build commands — do not retry `cargo test` alone.

Canonical source comments: `aggregator/program/tests/spamm_mollusk/main.rs` (header) and `common/env.rs` (`Env::new`).
